---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const endpoints = [
  {
    label: 'INTELLIGENCE',
    href: `${base}data/intelligence.json`,
    path: '/data/intelligence.json',
    description: 'Canonical published signals, active threads, predictions, evidence links, falsifiers, and limitations.',
  },
  {
    label: 'LLMS',
    href: `${base}llms.txt`,
    path: '/llms.txt',
    description: 'Small discovery entry point for agents: canonical JSON, change feed, schemas, record resources, and interpretation rules.',
  },
  { label: 'CHANGES', href: `${base}data/changes.json`, path: '/data/changes.json', description: 'Complete post-migration stream. Filter by sequence, not source publication date.' },
  { label: 'HISTORY', href: `${base}data/history.json`, path: '/data/history.json', description: 'Accepted events and immutable legacy snapshot reference.' },
  { label: 'ATOM', href: `${base}atom.xml`, path: '/atom.xml', description: 'Sitewide judgment revisions, corrections and reviews.' },
  {
    label: 'COVERAGE',
    href: `${base}data/coverage.json`,
    path: '/data/coverage.json',
    description: 'What GrepSignal reviewed in the current cycle, including publication and no-publish outcomes.',
  },
  {
    label: 'VERSION SCHEMA',
    href: `${base}schema/record-version.schema.json`,
    path: '/schema/record-version.schema.json',
    description: 'Immutable record-version snapshot envelope for stable citations.',
  },
  {
    label: 'INTELLIGENCE SCHEMA',
    href: `${base}schema/intelligence.schema.json`,
    path: '/schema/intelligence.schema.json',
    description: 'JSON Schema for the canonical intelligence payload.',
  },
  { label: 'HISTORY SCHEMA', href: `${base}schema/history.schema.json`, path: '/schema/history.schema.json', description: 'Versioned event envelope; lifecycle invariants also enforced during build.' },
  {
    label: 'COVERAGE SCHEMA',
    href: `${base}schema/coverage.schema.json`,
    path: '/schema/coverage.schema.json',
    description: 'JSON Schema for the coverage payload.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="For agents — GrepSignal"
  description="Machine-readable GrepSignal intelligence, schemas, evidence conventions, and guidance for AI agents."
>
  <main>
    <section class="agent-hero">
      <div class="wrap agent-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">&gt; grep --machine-readable</div>
          <h1>For agents.</h1>
          <p>
            GrepSignal is static-first and JSON-first. Use the structured public artifacts as the canonical interface;
            treat HTML as a human presentation layer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-card" aria-label="Recommended agent entry point">
          <span class="terminal-label">START HERE</span>
          <code>GET {base}data/intelligence.json</code>
          <a href={`${base}data/intelligence.json`}>Open canonical intelligence →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="wrap agent-content">
      <section aria-labelledby="endpoints-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="section-kicker">DISCOVERY</span>
            <h2 id="endpoints-title">Public machine-readable artifacts</h2>
          </div>
          <small>No auth. No runtime API. Static public snapshots.</small>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-list">
          {endpoints.map((endpoint) => (
            <a class="endpoint-row" href={endpoint.href}>
              <div>
                <span class="endpoint-label">{endpoint.label}</span>
                <code>{endpoint.path}</code>
              </div>
              <p>{endpoint.description}</p>
              <span class="endpoint-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-grid" aria-label="Agent consumption guidance">
        <article class="guide-card">
          <span class="section-kicker">CONSUME</span>
          <h2>Recommended flow</h2><p>Intelligence now uses schema v2. Arrays retain withdrawn/replaced records: inspect lifecycle and assessment before recommending them. Version 0 is a legacy snapshot, not complete earlier event history. Save the latest sequence and process each larger sequence; timestamps are not safe cursors. First-publication times remain null until explicitly verified. See Changes and Editorial policy for corrections and reuse.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Discover once.</strong> <code>/llms.txt</code> points to the canonical machine interfaces and explains the time semantics.</li>
            <li><strong>Fetch JSON first.</strong> Use <code>/data/intelligence.json</code> for a full snapshot, or <code>/data/signals/&#123;id&#125;.json</code>, <code>/data/threads/&#123;id&#125;.json</code>, and <code>/data/predictions/&#123;id&#125;.json</code> for one record.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the contract.</strong> Read <code>schema_version</code> and validate against the public schema when strict parsing matters.</li>
            <li><strong>Use stable IDs and version citations.</strong> Current record JSON exposes <code>cite_as</code> and an immutable <code>record_version_permalink</code>. Version snapshots freeze derived context at their <code>snapshot_sequence</code>; current derived relations may move later.</li>
            <li><strong>Use derived links as context.</strong> Signals expose <code>thread_ids</code>; Threads expose <code>signal_ids</code>. Typed relation fields preserve supporting vs. contradicting context.</li>
            <li><strong>Follow evidence.</strong> Use source links to inspect primary or affected-party evidence when a claim matters. <code>retrieved_at: null</code> means GrepSignal did not record a retrieval time; do not infer one. <code>lineage_id</code> groups URLs that derive from the same underlying evidence event when that lineage is known.</li>
            <li><strong>Use public receipts.</strong> Change events expose proposal provenance, deterministic <code>changed_fields</code> for revisions, and a public acceptance receipt with an event hash even when the operational review reference points to the private engine.</li>
            <li><strong>Carry uncertainty forward.</strong> Preserve falsifiers, limitations, status, and prediction resolution instead of flattening them into a definitive claim.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article class="guide-card">
          <span class="section-kicker">BOUNDARIES</span>
          <h2>Interpretation rules</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Published signals are curated material changes, not a complete news feed.</li>
            <li>Absence from the dataset does not imply an event did not happen or is unimportant.</li>
            <li>Coverage records describe what was reviewed; they are useful for distinguishing “not reviewed” from “reviewed, not published.”</li>
            <li>Discovery channels may prioritize research, but factual claims should be traced to the linked evidence.</li>
            <li>Do not treat probability as certainty. Predictions remain accountable to their deadline and resolution state.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="contract-section" aria-labelledby="contract-title">
        <div>
          <span class="section-kicker">CONTRACT</span>
          <h2 id="contract-title">What a signal carries</h2>
          <p>
            The canonical record is designed to preserve both the synthesis and the conditions under which that synthesis could be wrong.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="contract-fields">
          <code>id</code>
          <code>type</code>
          <code>status</code>
          <code>summary</code>
          <code>why_it_matters</code>
          <code>second_order_effect</code>
          <code>watch_next</code>
          <code>falsifiers[]</code>
          <code>limitations[]</code>
          <code>sources[]</code>
          <code>thread_ids[]</code>
          <code>thread_relations[]</code>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="agent-policy" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
        <div>
          <span class="section-kicker">USAGE</span>
          <h2 id="policy-title">Link to evidence. Don’t mirror it.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            GrepSignal publishes original synthesis and source metadata, not mirrored article bodies. Agents should keep that boundary:
            cite or follow the original evidence URL when deeper source detail is required instead of reconstructing third-party content from GrepSignal.
          </p>
          <p>
            The canonical language is English. Consumers may translate for their own users, but should keep the public IDs and source URLs unchanged.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="agent-footer-card">
        <div>
          <span class="section-kicker">SOURCE</span>
          <h2>Inspect the publication layer</h2>
          <p>The public repository contains the site, schemas, validation, and approved publication-safe data.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="github-link" href="https://github.com/cinic0101/grepsignal">View GrepSignal on GitHub →</a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap footerline">
      <span>GrepSignal — structured intelligence for humans and agents.</span>
      <span>Link to evidence. Don’t mirror it.</span>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .agent-hero { padding: 78px 0 58px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .agent-hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(300px, .65fr); gap: 64px; align-items: end; }
  .agent-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(58px, 8vw, 96px); }
  .agent-hero p { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; font-size: 20px; color: #383733; }
  .terminal-card { border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--panel); padding: 22px; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .terminal-label { font: 800 10px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--accent); }
  .terminal-card code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; font: 650 13px/1.6 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .terminal-card a, .github-link { color: var(--accent); font: 800 11px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; text-decoration: none; }
  .terminal-card a:hover, .terminal-card a:focus-visible, .github-link:hover, .github-link:focus-visible { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .agent-content { padding-top: 54px; padding-bottom: 90px; }
  .endpoint-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .endpoint-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr) auto; gap: 30px; align-items: center; padding: 22px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-decoration: none; }
  .endpoint-row:hover .endpoint-arrow, .endpoint-row:focus-visible .endpoint-arrow { transform: translateX(4px); }
  .endpoint-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; color: var(--accent); font: 800 10px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .07em; }
  .endpoint-row code { font: 650 13px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .endpoint-row p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .endpoint-arrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: 22px; transition: transform .15s ease; }
  .guide-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 26px; margin-top: 56px; }
  .guide-card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 28px; }
  .guide-card h2, .contract-section h2, .agent-policy h2, .agent-footer-card h2 { margin: 5px 0 16px; font: 600 31px/1.08 Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .guide-card ol, .guide-card ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 21px; color: #3d3b36; }
  .guide-card li + li { margin-top: 13px; }
  .guide-card code { font-size: .88em; }
  .contract-section, .agent-policy { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(230px, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr); gap: 50px; }
  .contract-section p, .agent-policy p, .agent-footer-card p { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
  .agent-policy p + p { margin-top: 16px; }
  .contract-fields { display: flex; gap: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-content: flex-start; }
  .contract-fields code { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 7px; padding: 7px 9px; background: var(--panel); font: 650 11px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .agent-footer-card { margin-top: 56px; padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--panel); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 30px; align-items: end; }
  .agent-footer-card h2 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .agent-hero-grid, .guide-grid, .contract-section, .agent-policy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .endpoint-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 12px 20px; }
    .endpoint-row p { grid-column: 1; }
    .endpoint-arrow { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / span 2; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .agent-hero { padding: 58px 0 42px; }
    .agent-hero p { font-size: 18px; }
    .agent-content { padding-top: 38px; }
    .agent-footer-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .endpoint-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; }
  }
</style>